 "app_effect": {
  "source": "trial_prior_scenario",
  "form": "multiplier = max(0.05, 1 - r * (D - D_now) / delta_shannon_field) on drought loss cost, for D >= D_now (and 1 + r*(D_now - D)/delta for D < D_now)",
  "delta_shannon_field": 0.66,
  "r": {
   "est": 0.14,
   "lo": 0.0,
   "hi": 0.9
  },
  "label": "Scenario assumption from field trials (Bowles et al. 2020: 14-90% smaller maize drought-year yield losses in diversified rotations); est = trial lower bound, lo = no effect (the observational county estimate is not distinguishable from zero), hi = trial upper bound. Not estimated from the county data."
 },
 "verdict": "Data: 7463 corn county-years (2013-2024, 631 counties), 630 of them high-hazard (hazard_z > 1). Diversity varies mostly between counties: within-county SD 0.044 vs between-county SD 0.106 (16% of variance is within county). Raw: more diverse counties are drier/western (Spearman D vs longitude +0.01, vs JJA climatology -0.01, vs irrigation -0.12) and have higher mean corn drought loss cost (Spearman +0.05) - the raw association is confounded by climate. Headline (county FE + state-year FE, corn): effect of +0.1 Shannon in high-hazard years = -14.5% of mean loss cost (95% CI -51.1 to +22.0); PPML -1.6% (CI -100.0 to +2060333.0). Negative = protective. Bowles et al. 2020 trials: 14-90% smaller drought-year maize yield losses. Implied by the PPML estimate for the same corn-soy -> 4-crop contrast (+0.66 Shannon): 10% reduction (CI -2965692090819103358409366306816 to 100). Placebo, low-hazard years: D coefficient -0.0006 (CI -0.1667 to +0.1656). Verdict: the observational county-level effect is NOT distinguishable from zero once climate, soils and fixed effects are controlled. The data neither confirm nor rule out the trial effect at county scale. The app uses the field-trial range (Bowles et al. 2020) as a labelled scenario assumption, not as an estimate from these data."
}